From 8c384ff590c8bb3d04ffde9a5db21afd7914f195 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:08:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Merge dashboard Queue and Live Activity into one
 filterable panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The dashboard used to stack the Queue and Live Execution Feed as two
separate full-width sections, so seeing both meant scrolling past a
tall stats panel and a tall Queue just to reach the feed. It also had a
real data-duplication bug: a failed run with a confident auto-diagnosis
renders as an actionable Queue card (queue.ts's run_failure path) *and*
as a second, plainer row in the feed's own unfiltered runs query — same
skillRuns.id, shown twice on the same page.

mergeUnifiedActivity (src/lib/unified-activity.ts) combines both into
one sorted, de-duplicated list (needs-action first, then running, then
completed) and drops the feed-side duplicate whenever a queue item
already covers that run. UnifiedActivityPanel renders it as a fixed
client/product rail on the left, the filtered list in the middle, and
a detail pane that opens on the right as a real flex sibling (same
mechanics as right-utility-panel.tsx) that narrows the list column
instead of covering it — so switching between an overview and a
specific item's detail no longer means losing your place or leaving
the page.

Row actions reuse the exact mutations queue-panel.tsx and
overview-stats-panel.tsx already call (useQueueItemActions,
getRepairAction) rather than re-deriving them. queue-panel.tsx and
live-execution-feed.tsx are untouched behind their own full pages
(/dashboard/queue, /dashboard/runs) for anyone who needs the deeper
tag/grouping/pagination features — this is additive, not a rewrite.

Also fixes a real, separate gap while touching this code: both
components' module/skill filter chips only covered Showtime and
Reputation Manager, so Cold Open and Whop Agent runs displayed
correctly but had no chip to filter by. Both now build their chip
list from all four registered products (product-catalog.ts).

Consolidated the two now-redundant "Queue" and "Live Executions" tour
steps into one, since they point at the same element now.

